  id: ecuatorial
  nombre: Low equatorial
  descripcionBreve: Circles Mars near the equator at low altitude and passes over the anomaly region again and again.
  costoCr: 100
  periapsisKm: 300
  apoapsisKm: 300
  ventaja: "Repeated low passes over the anomaly (Gale crater, about 5\xB0 S)"
  limitacion: Never sees the poles
  datoNasa: "No Mars orbiter has flown a low equatorial orbit yet. An equatorial orbit only covers low latitudes; Gale crater, where Curiosity landed, is at about 5\xB0 S."
  datoNasaEs: "Ning\xFAn orbitador de Marte ha volado todav\xEDa una \xF3rbita ecuatorial baja. Una \xF3rbita ecuatorial solo cubre latitudes bajas; el cr\xE1ter Gale, donde aterriz\xF3 Curiosity, est\xE1 a unos 5\xB0 S."
  fuenteNasa: NASA/JPL
